  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000 for phase one, led by Sarah Tan. The project has progressed through various stages, including a design phase, a call for ideas by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization, and the establishment of strategic partnerships with TechInnovate. Significant progress has been made in phase two, achieving a breakthrough in predictive analytics, and the project reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing. Additional updates include a budget increase to $55,000 for the compliance plan, an approved $15,000 budget for specialized training, and a move into the development phase led by Omar Jensen. A detailed report on phase two progress is scheduled to be shared in a staff meeting on November 20th."
